437	// values that contain '&', '=', '%' and '+' the way a user does: the rule
438	// comes from the config file, the request from stdin, and the merged query is
439	// observed inside upstreamURL. The rule's name and value are literal text;
440	// on the wire only raw '&' separates fragments and the first raw '=' splits
441	// a fragment, so the encoded "&" and "=" never create extra parameters. Both
442	// sources of the same decoded name merge at the first hit's position while
